(Stage 1c — runtime type predicates. A mixed list iterated with an
 if/otherwise-if chain classifies each element by its per-slot type tag.
 Booleans (tag 3) must be distinguishable from numbers (tag 0) even though
 both print as numbers; `is a decimal` matches the float tag (2).
 Acceptance criteria 1, 2, and 5.)

a list called m is [1, "two", 3.5, yes].
For each item in m,
  if item is a text, print "text: {item}",
  otherwise if item is a decimal, print "decimal: {item}",
  otherwise if item is a boolean, print "boolean: {item}",
  otherwise print "number: {item}".